  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Ampliando el acceso a los servicios p&#xfa;blicos</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Municipal Service Delivery and Governance (TuMUNI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ecuador):  Although Ecuador&apos;s 2008 Constitution marked decentralization as a national priority, its implementation faces persistent challenges. Local governments struggle with inadequate revenue sources, over-reliance on national government transfers, and limited planning and management capacity, which hinder their ability to deliver essential public services. Mechanisms for citizen participation and transparency are underutilized, weakening local governance. Ecuador grapples with economic exclusion, citizen insecurity, and a lack of social cohesion-challenges that demand active local authority participation. Critical infrastructure gaps also persist, only 66 percent of the water supply and 31 percent of sanitation facilities are managed appropriately..USAID launched TuMUNI in September 2023. This activity aims to strengthen municipal ability to provide critical public services-particularly water and sanitation-while promoting transparent governance and fostering greater citizen participation in decision-making...TuMUNI will:.Enhance municipal fiscal management introducing good practices for budgeting and resource allocation.Promote citizen engagement and transparency.Train municipal officials to increase efficiency and effectiveness in service delivery.Strengthen water and sanitation institutions by technical assistance and training to improve management and expand access to safe water.Foster public-private partnerships to co-design, co-finance, and co-deliver interventions that ensure sustainable service delivery..TuMUNI will deliver measurable improvements in municipal governance, water and sanitation infrastructure, and citizen trust in local institutions. These achievements align with the Bolstering Democratic Reformers pillar of the Presidential Initiative for Democratic Renewal (PIDR), supporting Ecuador&apos;s democratic and sustainable development goals. This mechanism attributes $500,000 to PIDR... .........</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El prop&#xf3;sito de esta actividad es ampliar el acceso de los ciudadanos a servicios p&#xfa;blicos cr&#xed;ticos, incluido el agua, el saneamiento y la higiene (WASH), fortaleciendo la capacidad de los gobiernos locales para una actuaci&#xf3;n eficaz, transparente y con capacidad de respuesta ciudadana.</narrative>
  </description>
